.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VFS_START 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_start
.Nd make a filesystem operational
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/mount.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vfs_start "struct mount *mp" "int flags" "struct thread *td"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vfs_start
function is called after a mount is successfully completed to make the filesystem operational.
It calls the filesystem-specific VFS_START operation.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa flags"
.It Fa mp
The filesystem to start.
.It Fa flags
Mount flags.
.It Fa td
The thread performing the operation.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs_mount 9
